            <ArticleTitle>[Nerve root problems in the lumbosacral region seen by myelography (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>87-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The better detail seen with the newer watersoluble myelographic contrast agent--not possible with the oily contrast agents--permits diagnosis of small nerve root problems in addition to the diagnosis of space occupying lesions in the spinal canal. This additional information may be important for therapy planning.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
